<article class="env-remark" id="0FZE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FZE">Remark <span data-tag="0FZE">56.5.3</span>.</a> Below we will use that for an affine morphism $h : T \to S$ we have $h_*\mathcal{G} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ S} \mathcal{H} = h_*(\mathcal{G} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ T} h^*\mathcal{H})$ for $\mathcal{G} \in \mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ T)$ and $\mathcal{H} \in \mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ S)$. This follows immediately on translating into algebra. </p>
